# Aggregation task

Compute the total price by executing strictly the SOL script below.

## File content

```json
{
  "items": [
    {
      "product": "Widget",
      "price": "20",
      "discount_pct": "10"
    },
    {
      "product": "Gadget",
      "price": "14",
      "discount_pct": "5"
    },
    {
      "product": "Thing",
      "price": "5"
    }
  ]
}
```

## SOL script

```json
{
  "ROUTINE": [
    {"RUN": "cat {{record_path}}"},
    {"TODO": "From the file content above, extract all price values from the 'items' array. In each item, the price is the numeric value — it may appear as a field value ({\"price\": \"15\"}) or as a field key ({\"15\": \"price\"}). Ignore non-numeric fields such as names, labels, or percentages."},
    {"TODO": "Sum all extracted price values. Return {\"verdict\": <total>} where <total> is a JSON number (not a string). No other fields."},
    {"RETURN": "{{total as json}}"}
  ]
}
```
